Then lock the trail down: `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE ON audit_log FROM app_role` so even a compromised app can only append, never rewrite history — an audit table the app can edit isn't an audit table.

Left out of this sketch: retention/export policy, enriching entries with request metadata (IP, route) — which would need an app-side column since triggers only see DB state — and whether reads need logging too (you only asked about writes).

